{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>In plowing and in harvest.</b> Why are plowing and harvest mentioned? Some of our Sages say: it concerns the plowing of the eve of the seventh year that enters into the seventh year, and the harvest of the seventh year that goes out after the seventh year — to teach you that one adds from the profane onto the sacred. And so its meaning is: ״Six days you shall labor and on the seventh day you shall cease״ — yet of the labor of the six days that I permitted you, there is a year when plowing and harvest are forbidden. And there is no need to say plowing and harvest of the seventh year itself, for it is already stated ״your field you shall not sow״ etc. (Leviticus 25). And some say it speaks only of the Sabbath, and the plowing and harvest mentioned here come to tell you: just as plowing is optional, so too harvest is optional — excluding the harvest of the omer, which is a commandment and overrides the Sabbath (Rosh HaShanah 9)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:33.459868909Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}